<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct imported vehicle sales up 11.6% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct imported vehicle sales up 11.6% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Domestic sales of imported vehicles rose 11.6 percent in October from a year earlier to 33,550 units, the Japan Automobile Importers Association (JAIA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It was the second straight month of year-on-year gains after August's 2.9 percent decline, the first drop in 34 months.</p>
<p>Sales reached a record high for that month, surpassing the previous October record of 30,068 marked last year.</p>
<p>Sales of vehicles produced by overseas units of Japanese makers fell 26.7 percent to 7,040 in October.  </p>
<p>The October breakdown, with percentage changes from a year earlier, was as follows:</p>
<p>    Cars total		30,038  up   7.9 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2000 cc   20,489  up   0.7 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc   9,549  up  27.7 percent</p>
